course: dictionary
lesson: 7040
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as numbered senses. «Party» is a good example: it can be a fun get-together, a group of people doing something together, or a political group. The words around it show you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Read the context first. «Lily invited girls from both streets to her birthday, and her mum had to buy twice as many party bags.» The clues are birthday and party bags, so party means a fun get-together. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence. It still makes sense.
explain: Party can also be a verb. In ««Then she misses her mate's party»», party is a noun, a thing that happens. The verb is to party, which means to have fun at a party. Its forms change: party, parties, partied, partying.
explain: Sometimes the meaning is a group. A search party is a group of people who go out together to find someone lost. Other kinds of party, such as a political party, are groups who share ideas about running a country.
fact: A word with more than one meaning can be understood by checking the words around it.
fact: «Party» can mean a fun event where people eat, play and have fun.
fact: «Party» can also mean a group of people doing something together, like a search party.
fact: A political party is a group of people who share ideas about how to run a country.
fact: To party is a verb: it means to have fun at a party.
exercise: «Lily invited girls from both streets to her birthday, and her mum had to buy twice as many party bags.» In this sentence, party means what? | To argue loudly | A group who share ideas about running a country | *A fun get-together with food and games | A group of people searching for someone
exercise: «A search party went up the hill to find the lost boy.» What does party mean here? | To have fun | *A group of people doing one job together | A group who share ideas about running a country | A birthday get-together
exercise: Which word shows the past form of the verb to party? Lily ___ all night long. | *partied | party | partying | parties
test: «Tariq's dad says no to a sleepover party, then drives Tariq there.» Which meaning of party fits here? | *A get-together with friends | A group who share ideas about running a country | A tool for blowing | A group of people searching for someone
test: Which describes a political party? | A birthday with party bags and games | *A group of people who share ideas about how to run a country | A search team looking for a lost walker | To have fun at a party
exam: In «Kyiv... 1982 is a chosen round date, like a party for a grandad who lost his birth certificate», what kind of party is meant? | A group of tourists | A political party | *A celebration, like a birthday party | A search party
